  "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n- Split stock construction into private `stock_sim/backend_build.rs`, keeping `Stock` and its existing public API in place.\r\n- Split swept-solid evaluation and conservative window bounds into private `stock_sim/field_sweep.rs`. Keep the existing crate-internal `field_cut::Sweep` path through a `pub(crate)` re-export.\r\n- Preserve the existing algorithms, constants, diagnostics, refusal checks, test sources, goldens, manifests, and dependencies. Record the decision in `RECOMMENDED.md`.\r\n\r\nResulting physical line counts: `backend.rs` 311, `backend_build.rs` 156, `field_cut.rs` 242, `field_sweep.rs` 211. All 30 existing function definitions compare identical to the baseline after line-ending normalization; independent static review found no behavior/API/privacy/module-registration defect.\r\n\r\n## Readings and provenance\r\n\r\nRead the current `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, stock-simulation module contracts/callers, relevant test gate maps, and local gate script. This is code movement from existing CamCraft modules, not a new algorithm or external/vendor implementation. Both new modules carry provenance headers.\r\n\r\n## Historical validation (original published head 052aa6e)\n\r\nNative Windows/MSVC, Rust/Cargo 1.99.1, on the exact reviewed candidate tree:\r\n\r\n- `cargo test --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-sim -- --test-threads=6`: **208 passed, 0 failed**.\r\n- `cargo test --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-app --test stock_engine_agreement --test stock_export --test stock_field_cost --test stock_play --test stock_sim_document --test stock_view --test lathe_field_sim -- --test-threads=6`: **28 passed, 0 failed, 4 existing heavy tests ignored**.\r\n- `cargo clippy --locked -j 6 -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: **passed**.\r\n- Repository quick gate (`scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base bf3519b09176dea3d54b586c2290ae7f6e0550b5`): **passed all 3 steps; 170 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored**.\r\n- Independent spec/code-quality static review and `git diff --check`: **passed**.\r\n\r\nThe same sim and selected app suites also passed on the pre-refactor baseline. Pinning suites include `stock_backend_parity`, `stock_sdf_cut`, `stock_lathe`, `lathe_field_sim`, `stock_export`, `stock_play`, `stock_sim_document`, and `stock_view`; none was weakened or changed.\r\n\r\nAn initial quick-gate invocation included a stray positional `.` and selected a nonexistent test filter, so it ran no tests; its failure is preserved separately, not counted as a passing gate.\r\n\r\nNot run: ignored/heavy release lanes or full-workspace/UI validation. `graphify update` was unavailable because the tool and generated local graph were absent; no graph output was fabricated or committed. No hosted workflows or release tags were triggered.\r\n\r\n## Review follow-up: synchronized branch\n\n- Addressed the sole requested integration item: merged upstream main at `9bb8d266846f37378a9ed8edcb85c64afc9be4a0` into the same feature branch and normal-pushed final head `4b2a32be69b1f8e3c221e67b8a6e7ead01ad1eff` (tree `c8251607dfebff71144bbfb22dad42f8c4242a34`).\n- Preserved all upstream `RECOMMENDED.md` bytes and the exact original 17-line issue entry. The four moved source-file blobs are unchanged from the reviewed original head; `mod.rs` preserves upstream exports and adds only the two private module registrations relative to the synchronized base.\n- Ran the requested quick tier exactly once on this final head: `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -File scripts/gate.ps1 -Tier quick -Base 9bb8d266846f37378a9ed8edcb85c64afc9be4a0`. **Native exit 0; all 3 steps passed; 177 passed, 0 failed, 2 ignored across 16 test summaries.**\n- Independent incremental integration review found no required correction; `git diff --check` passed; candidate head/tree remained clean and unchanged.\n- No additional full simulation/application suites, baseline, or Clippy runs for this update. The full-suite results above are explicitly historical.\n- No hosted workflows, force push, protected-main merge, release, or tag. Final approval and merge remain with the maintainer.\n\nChangelog: Split stock-simulation construction and swept-solid evaluation into focused internal modules; no behavior or public API changes.\r\n\r\nFixes #61\r\n",
